12. Data Science Methodologies
Data science techniques can be used in later stages of the project to develop predictive and optimization capabilities.
12.1 Classification
Classification can be used to predict whether an order is likely to experience delivery risk.
The Late_delivery_risk variable can potentially be used as the target variable.
Possible algorithms include:
•	Logistic Regression
•	Decision Tree
•	Random Forest
Potential evaluation metrics include:
•	Accuracy
•	Precision
•	Recall
•	F1-score
•	ROC-AUC

12.2 Regression
Regression can be used to predict continuous logistics outcomes such as:
•	Delivery time
•	Transportation cost
•	Order profitability
For example, a regression model could estimate expected delivery time based on shipping mode, geographical region, order quantity, and other available features.

12.3 Clustering
Clustering can be used to group regions, customers, products, or orders with similar characteristics.
For example, K-Means clustering could be used to group regions according to:
•	Shipment volume
•	Average shipping time
•	Delivery risk
•	Sales
This can help management identify similar operational segments.

12.4 Optimization
Optimization techniques can be explored to support logistics decisions such as:
•	Shipping-mode selection
•	Resource allocation
•	Delivery planning
•	Cost reduction
•	Delay reduction
The objective would be to identify operational decisions that reduce delays and costs while maintaining acceptable service levels.

