14. Python Code Illustration
The following example demonstrates how the KPI analysis was performed.
kpi_summary = pd.DataFrame({
    "KPI": [
        "Total Orders",
        "Total Order Records",
        "Total Quantity Sold",
        "Total Sales",
        "Average Actual Shipping Time",
        "Average Scheduled Shipping Time",
        "Average Schedule Deviation",
        "On-Time Delivery Rate"
    ],
    "Value": [
        df["Order Id"].nunique(),
        len(df),
        df["Order Item Quantity"].sum(),
        df["Order Item Total"].sum(),
        round(df["Days for shipping (real)"].mean(), 2),
        round(df["Days for shipment (scheduled)"].mean(), 2),
        round(
            df["Days for shipping (real)"].mean()
            - df["Days for shipment (scheduled)"].mean(),
            2
        ),
        round(
            (df["Late_delivery_risk"] == 0).mean() * 100,
            2
        )
    ]
})

print(kpi_summary)
Example shipping-mode analysis:
shipping_analysis = (
    df.groupby("Shipping Mode")
      .agg(
          shipments=("Order Id", "count"),
          avg_actual_days=("Days for shipping (real)", "mean"),
          avg_scheduled_days=("Days for shipment (scheduled)", "mean"),
          late_risk_rate=("Late_delivery_risk", "mean")
      )
      .reset_index()
)

shipping_analysis["late_risk_rate"] *= 100

print(shipping_analysis)

15. Key Business Insights
The initial analysis produced several important insights:
1.	Actual shipping time was higher than scheduled shipping time by approximately 0.57 days on average.
2.	Significant differences were observed in delivery-risk levels across shipping modes.
3.	First Class showed the highest late-delivery-risk rate at 95.32%.
4.	Second Class also showed a relatively high late-delivery-risk rate of 76.63%.
5.	Standard Class showed a lower late-delivery-risk rate of 38.07% in the dataset.
6.	Central Africa had the highest late-delivery-risk rate among the analyzed regions at 57.96%.
7.	Several geographical regions showed late-risk rates above 55%, indicating areas that may require additional investigation.
8.	Shipping mode and geographical region appear to be potentially useful variables for future predictive modeling.

16. Strategic Recommendations
Based on the initial findings, the following recommendations are proposed:
16.1 Investigate High-Risk Shipping Modes
The organization should investigate why First Class and Second Class shipments show relatively high delivery-risk rates.
16.2 Analyze Regional Bottlenecks
High-risk regions should be examined further to identify possible transportation, scheduling, or operational constraints.
16.3 Monitor Schedule Deviation
The difference between actual and scheduled shipping time should be monitored as an operational KPI.
16.4 Develop Predictive Monitoring
A classification model can be developed in later stages to identify orders that may have a higher probability of delivery risk.
16.5 Use Data-Driven Resource Allocation
Predictive insights can eventually be combined with optimization techniques to support better shipping and resource-allocation decisions.

