18. Conclusion
The Week 1 task established the strategic foundation for a logistics data analytics project. A publicly available supply-chain dataset was selected and analyzed using Python-based tools.
The initial analysis identified important logistics KPIs and revealed meaningful differences in delivery-risk levels across shipping modes and geographical regions. The analysis also showed an average difference of 0.57 days between actual and scheduled shipping times.
The findings demonstrate how data analytics can be used to identify operational bottlenecks and support evidence-based decision-making. The next stages of the project will focus on cleaning and preprocessing the data, conducting advanced exploratory analysis, developing predictive models, and exploring optimization approaches.
Overall, the project provides a structured pathway from raw logistics data to actionable business insights and predictive decision support.

